{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"HeadwireGATTContract","externalID":"HeadwireGATTContract","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireGATTContract"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The GATT identifiers and characteristic values the iPad publishes and the Mac helper reads.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/GATTContract"],"title":"Identifiers","anchor":"Identifiers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeRequest","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeWireError"],"title":"Source mode","anchor":"Source-mode"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOffer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingAnswer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOfferWireError"],"title":"Pairing","anchor":"Pairing"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The iPad app and the Mac helper ship separately, so the identifiers and value formats they share live here in one Foundation-only module, and the helper links none of the HID code. HeadwireGATTContract owns the service and characteristic UUIDs, the source mode request the iPad publishes to ask the Mac for a video mode, and the pairing offer and answer that let the helper link pair over an encrypted Bluetooth link with no code. Each value starts with a version byte, and readers ignore bytes they do not know. It does not publish anything or talk to CoreBluetooth; HeadwireHID publishes the services, and the helper reads them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://HeadwireGATTContract/documentation/HeadwireGATTContract/PairingOfferWireError":{"url":"\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract\/pairingofferwireerror","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PairingOfferWireError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why a pairing offer or answer value could not be read."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOfferWireError","role":"symbol","title":"PairingOfferWireError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PairingOfferWireError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HeadwireGATTContract/documentation/HeadwireGATTContract/GATTContract":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The GATT identifiers the iPad publishes and the Mac helper reads, in one place, so the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sides, which ship separately, cannot drift."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GATTContract","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GATTContract","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/GATTContract","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GATTContract","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract\/gattcontract"},"doc://HeadwireGATTContract/documentation/HeadwireGATTContract/PairingAnswer":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingAnswer","url":"\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract\/pairinganswer","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the helper writes back: its own key fingerprint and the addresses its link listens on."}],"title":"PairingAnswer","navigatorTitle":[{"kin